# Complaint Template Gold Standard

Every sticky note must be **chart-ready**: click-to-insert without editing. If it does not sound like real clinician documentation, it fails.

## Section rules

| Section | Must be | Prohibited |
|---------|---------|------------|
| **HPI** | Patient story (onset, location, quality, duration, associated symptoms) | `*Reviewed`, `*Considered`, provider reasoning |
| **ROS** | Present symptoms, denied symptoms, red flags | Provider reasoning, `reviewed` |
| **Physical exam** | Observed findings only | History items, `reviewed` |
| **Reassessment** | Treatment response (improved, tolerated PO, resolved) | Data review language |
| **MDM — data reviewed** | `CBC reviewed`, `CT reviewed`, `troponin reviewed` | — |
| **MDM — reasoning/plan** | Working assessment, risk, impression, provider actions | Generic MDM only |

`reviewed` belongs only in **mdmDataReviewed** and **reassessment** (treatment response), not HPI/ROS/exam.

## Mandatory MDM stack (complaint-specific)

Every complaint family needs dedicated chips for: Working Assessment, Differential (common + serious + cannot-miss), Data Reviewed, Risk Stratification, Medical Reasoning, Impression, Plan.

Reference patterns: `providerDocumentationGiComplaintIntelligence19Mdm2.ts`, `providerDocumentationDehydrationViralIllnessComplaintIntelGoldStandard.ts`, `providerDocumentationComplaintIntelligenceWorkspaceChips.ts`.

## Workspace rendering (MDM.1)

Complaint-intelligence MDM chips must render as first-class click-to-insert groups in `ProviderDocumentationWorkspace` via `COMPLAINT_INTEL_MDM_CHIP_BINDINGS` and `COMPLAINT_INTEL_IMPRESSION_CHIP_BINDINGS`. No gold-standard MDM content may exist only in intel bundles without workspace chip rendering.

## Three-track hardening (required for ME.2* and beyond)

- **Track A** — Sticky-note governance (wrong-domain denial)
- **Track B** — MDM reinforcement (full complaint-specific MDM stack)
- **Track C** — Human documentation audit (patient story, ROS, exam, reassessment, reasoning, plan tests)

## Good vs bad HPI examples

```
✅ began today | sudden onset | sore throat | odynophagia | drooling
❌ dysphagia reviewed | fever reviewed | symptom duration reviewed
```

## Good vs bad exam examples

```
✅ tonsillar erythema | uvular deviation | peritonsillar fullness | airway patent
❌ tonsillar findings if documented | airway findings reviewed
```

When adding or changing complaint intel keys, update matching `en.ts` and `fr.ts` message files. French product strings in `fr.ts`.
